Q: cli curl to php curl for uploading file A: <p>I know it's a 12 years old questions but it appears first on google and didn't find any answer elsewhere so I want to share the code I've made working for me. The main problem was it has to be a PUT method and not a POST one.</p>
<pre><code>$url = 'https://s3.us.archive.org/sam-s3-test-08/demo-intro-to-k.pdf';
$file = 'intro-to-k.pdf'; //in my case file in the same directory than the script

$fh_res = fopen($file, 'rb');

$ch = curl_init();
$headers = array();
$headers[] = 'Authorization: LOW accesskey:secret';
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER, $headers);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, $url);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_PUT, 1);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_INFILE, $fh_res);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_INFILESIZE, filesize($file));
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, 1);
$response = curl_exec ($ch);
curl_close($ch);
fclose($fh_res);
echo $response;
</code></pre>
<p>$response is empty if the upload is a success. Or it displays any error.</p>
